# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env, adjacent to this checkout.
#
# Each entry is `name=ref`, which clones `ref` directly. Without the `=ref`
# half, clone-siblings resolves the revision from a per-commit WORKSPACE lock
# published to the manifests repo — a workspace-level lock-storage opt-in this
# project does not use. Reprobuild's vanilla behaviour is the solved-graph
# `repro.lock` committed in this repo; there is no manifests-repo record for
# any commit here, so every lane failed in `Setup dev env` before reaching a
# build. Pinning the ref keeps the workspace lock out of the path entirely.
#
# `dev` is each sibling's mainline, which is what this recorder is developed
# and tested against: the Nim writer's sources are compiled into
# `codetracer_trace_writer_nim`'s static library at cargo build time, so the
# two must be the pair the tests were written for.
codetracer-trace-format=dev
codetracer-trace-format-nim=dev
